# The natural-language-to-scryfall-filters service backing /magic-tools is
# reached same-origin at /api — the Vite dev server proxies it to localhost:8080
# and Firebase Hosting rewrites it to Cloud Run in production — so this is
# normally left unset.
#
# Setting it points a local build at a deployed instance, which is a
# cross-origin call — and the service no longer sends CORS headers at all, so
# a browser will block that. Use it for curl or a non-browser client; to
# exercise a deployed backend from the site, change the Vite proxy target
# instead and stay same-origin.
# VITE_TRANSLATE_API_URL=https://your-service.run.app
